BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6671fcc63e24604a@jdpi.pages.dev
DTSTAMP:20261030T060403Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19900304
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19900305
SUMMARY:1990 Russian Supreme Soviet election (Soviet Union / Russia)
DESCRIPTION:Legislative elections were held in the Russian SFSR in March 19
 90 as part of the regional elections across the Soviet Union. The first ro
 und was held on 4 March\, and the second round on 14\, 17 and 18 March. Me
 mbers of the Communist Party of the Soviet Union (CPSU) won 920 of the 1\,
 068 seats\, although several were supporters of the Democratic Russia move
 ment.\n\nElection: Soviet Union / Russia\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org
 /wiki/1990_Russian_Supreme_Soviet_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)
 \, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
CATEGORIES:Election
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1990_Russian_Supreme_Soviet_election
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f404989520405147@jdpi.pages.dev
DTSTAMP:20261030T060403Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19900304
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19900305
SUMMARY:1990 Ukrainian Supreme Soviet election (Soviet Union / Russia)
DESCRIPTION:Supreme Soviet elections were held in the Ukrainian SSR on 4 Ma
 rch 1990\, with runoffs in some seats held between 10 and 18 March. The el
 ections were held to elect deputies to the republic's parliament\, the Ver
 khovna Rada. Simultaneously\, elections of oblast councils also took place
  in their respective administrative divisions.\n\nElection: Soviet Union /
  Russia\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1990_Ukrainian_Supreme_Sovi
 et_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
CATEGORIES:Election
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1990_Ukrainian_Supreme_Soviet_election
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:974623ccccf444bc@jdpi.pages.dev
DTSTAMP:20261030T060403Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19900310
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19900311
SUMMARY:Hérard Abraham takes power (Haiti)
DESCRIPTION:Hérard Abraham was a Haitian military officer and politician w
 ho served as acting President of Haiti between 10 March 1990 and 13 March 
 1990.\n\nNew leader: Haiti\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/H%C3%A9r
 ard_Abraham\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
CATEGORIES:New leader
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/H%C3%A9rard_Abraham
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
