SUMMARY:1990 Armenian Supreme Soviet election (Soviet Union / Russia)
DESCRIPTION:Parliamentary elections were held in the Armenian SSR on 20 May
  1990\, with further rounds held on 3 June and 15 July due to low turnouts
  invalidating earlier results. By 21 July\, 64 seats were still unfilled\,
  with 16 still unfilled in February the following year. The result was a v
 ictory for the Communist Party of Armenia\, which won 136 of the 259 seats
 .\n\nElection: Soviet Union / Russia\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wik
 i/1990_Armenian_Supreme_Soviet_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, 
 via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
