SUMMARY:1990 Hungarian presidential election referendum (Hungary)
DESCRIPTION:A referendum on introducing direct elections for the Presidency
  was held in Hungary on 29 July 1990. Although the proposal was supported 
 by 86% of voters\, voter turnout was just 14%\, resulting in the referendu
 m being declared invalid. As a result\, the President continued to be elec
 ted by the National Assembly.\n\nReferendum: Hungary\nSource: https://en.w
 ikipedia.org/wiki/1990_Hungarian_presidential_election_referendum\nText: W
 ikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
