SUMMARY:1990 Hungarian presidential election (Hungary)
DESCRIPTION:The first indirect presidential election was held in Hungary on
  3 August 1990\, following the transition to multi-party democracy. Incumb
 ent Speaker of the National Assembly and acting head of state Árpád Gön
 cz was elected as president with more than three-quarter majority.\n\nElec
 tion: Hungary\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1990_Hungarian_presid
 ential_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev)
