SUMMARY:1990 Irish presidential election (Ireland)
DESCRIPTION:The 1990 Irish presidential election was the tenth presidential
  election to be held in Ireland\, the fifth to be contested by more than o
 ne candidate\, and the first to have a female candidate and winner. It was
  held on Wednesday 7 November 1990\, and was won by Mary Robinson on a joi
 nt Labour Party and Workers' Party ticket.\n\nElection: Ireland\nSource: h
