DESCRIPTION:The 1990 Chadian coup d'état took place on 1 December 1990 whe
 n the forces of the Patriotic Salvation Movement (MPS)\, a Libyan–backed
  rebel group under the leadership of General Idriss Déby\, entered the Ch
 adian capital N'Djamena unopposed. The MPS troops entered Chad by crossing
  the Sudanese border three weeks earlier.\n\nCoup: Chad\nSource: https://e
 n.wikipedia.org/wiki/1990_Chadian_coup_d%27%C3%A9tat\nText: Wikipedia (CC 
