SUMMARY:1991 Barbadian general election (Barbados)
DESCRIPTION:General elections were held in Barbados on 22 January 1991 to e
 lect all 28 members (MPs) of the House of Assembly of Barbados. The result
  was a victory for the ruling Democratic Labour Party (DLP)\, which won 18
  of the 28 seats. The opposition Barbados Labour Party led by Henry Forde 
 won ten seats\, an increase of seven compared to the 1986 elections.\n\nEl
 ection: Barbados\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1991_Barbadian_gen
 eral_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
