SUMMARY:Treaty signed: Brioni Agreement
DESCRIPTION:The Brioni Agreement\, also known as the Brioni Declaration is 
 a document signed by representatives of Slovenia\, Croatia\, and Yugoslavi
 a under the political sponsorship of the European Community (EC) on the Br
 ijuni Islands on 7 July 1991. The agreement sought to create an environmen
 t in which further negotiations on the future of Yugoslavia could take pla
 ce.\n\nTreaty: International\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brioni
 _Agreement\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
