DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19910819
SUMMARY:1991 Mexican legislative election (Mexico)
DESCRIPTION:Legislative elections were held in Mexico on 18 August 1991\, a
 longside gubernatorial elections in six states. The Institutional Revoluti
 onary Party (PRI) won 320 of the 500 seats in the Chamber of Deputies and 
 31 of the 32 seats up for election in the Senate. Voter turnout was 61% in
  the Chamber election and 62% in the Senate election.\n\nElection: Mexico\
 nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1991_Mexican_legislative_election\n
 Text: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
