DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19910831
SUMMARY:1991 Sierra Leonean constitutional referendum
DESCRIPTION:A referendum on a new constitution was held in Sierra Leone in 
 August 1991. Voting was held over four days. The new constitution would re
 store multi-party politics\, as the country had been a one-party state sin
 ce the 1978 constitutional referendum made the All People's Congress the o
 nly legally permitted party.\n\nReferendum: Sierra Leone\nSource: https://
 en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1991_Sierra_Leonean_constitutional_referendum\nText:
  Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
