SUMMARY:1992 Albanian parliamentary election
DESCRIPTION:Parliamentary elections were held in Albania on 22 March 1992\,
  with a second round of voting for eleven seats on 29 March. The result wa
 s a victory for the opposition Democratic Party of Albania\, which won 92 
 of the 140 seats. After the elections Aleksandër Meksi became prime minis
 ter and Sali Berisha became president.\n\nElection: Albania\nSource: https
 ://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1992_Albanian_parliamentary_election\nText: Wikip
 edia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
