SUMMARY:1992 Danish Maastricht Treaty referendum (Denmark)
DESCRIPTION:A referendum on the Maastricht Treaty for the founding of the E
 uropean Union was held in Denmark on 2 June 1992. The treaty was rejected 
 by 50.7% of voters with a turnout of 83.1%. This meant a serious hurdle on
  the way in the process of further European integration\, which neverthele
 ss did continue because all twelve member states did want to ratify.\n\nRe
 ferendum: Denmark\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1992_Danish_Maast
 richt_Treaty_referendum\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pa
