DESCRIPTION:Presidential elections were held in Croatia for the first time 
 on 2 August 1992 alongside simultaneous parliamentary elections. The resul
 t was a victory for incumbent Franjo Tuđman of the Croatian Democratic Un
 ion (HDZ)\, who received 58% of the vote\, becoming the first popularly el
 ected president of Croatia. Voter turnout was 75%.\n\nElection: Croatia\nS
 ource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1992_Croatian_presidential_election\n
