DESCRIPTION:Presidential elections were held in Estonia on 20 September 199
 2\, alongside parliamentary elections. As no candidate received over 50% o
 f the vote\, a second round was held in Parliament on 5 October 1992\, in 
 which Lennart Meri was elected. Voter turnout in the public vote was 68%.\
