SUMMARY:1993 Polish parliamentary election (Poland)
DESCRIPTION:Parliamentary elections were held in Poland on 19 September 199
 3. All 460 members of the Sejm and 100 senators of the Senate were elected
 . The elections were won by the left-wing parties of the Democratic Left A
 lliance and the Polish People's Party\, who formed a coalition government.
  The coalition was just four seats short of a supermajority.\n\nElection: 
 Poland\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1993_Polish_parliamentary_el
 ection\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
