SUMMARY:1993 Azerbaijani presidential election
DESCRIPTION:Presidential elections were held in Azerbaijan on 3 October 199
 3\, nearly four months after the June 1993 coup d'état. The result was a 
 victory for incumbent president Heydar Aliyev of the New Azerbaijan Party\
 , who won with nearly 99% of the vote. Election monitors characterized the
  elections as neither free nor fair.\n\nElection: Azerbaijan\nSource: http
 s://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1993_Azerbaijani_presidential_election\nText: Wi
 kipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
