DESCRIPTION:Presidential elections were held in Belarus on 23 June 1994\, w
 ith a second round on 10 July. They were the first national elections held
  in Belarus since the country seceded from the Soviet Union three years ea
 rlier. The result was an overwhelming victory for Alexander Lukashenko\, w
 ho received 81% of the vote in the second round.\n\nElection: Belarus\nSou
 rce: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1994_Belarusian_presidential_election\n
