SUMMARY:1994 Barbadian general election (Barbados)
DESCRIPTION:Early general elections were held in Barbados on 6 September 19
 94. The result was a victory for the opposition Barbados Labour Party\, wh
 ich won 19 of the 28 seats\, with its leader Owen Arthur becoming prime mi
 nister. The ruling Democratic Labour Party led by David Thompson was reduc
 ed to only eight seats.\n\nElection: Barbados\nSource: https://en.wikipedi
 a.org/wiki/1994_Barbadian_general_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)
 \, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
