SUMMARY:1994 Danish general election (Denmark)
DESCRIPTION:General elections were held in Denmark on 21 September 1994. Th
 e coalition of the Social Democratic Party\, the Danish Social Liberal Par
 ty and the Centre Democrats led by Poul Nyrup Rasmussen remained in power 
 despite the Christian People's Party\, which had been part of the governme
 nt\, failing to cross the 2% threshold and losing all four seats.\n\nElect
