SUMMARY:1994 Slovak parliamentary election (Slovakia)
DESCRIPTION:Early parliamentary elections were held in Slovakia on 30 Septe
 mber and 1 October 1994\, the first after the country's independence on 1 
 January 1993. Regular elections were scheduled to be held in 1996. However
 \, in March 1994 the government of Vladimír Mečiar lost a no-confidence 
 vote\, and a temporary coalition government led by Jozef Moravčík took o
 ver.\n\nElection: Slovakia\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1994_Slo
