DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19950616
SUMMARY:21st G7 summit (Canada)
DESCRIPTION:The 21st G7 summit was held on June 15–17\, 1995 in Halifax\,
  Nova Scotia\, Canada. The venue for this summit meeting was Summit Place 
 in Halifax. It was labelled by Prime Minister Jean Chrétien as a "Chevrol
 et Summit"\, using a utilitarian automobile as a metaphor for the summit b
 eing less expensive than previous summits in Versailles and Venice.\n\nSum
 mit: Canada\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/21st_G7_summit\nText: W
 ikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
