DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19950730
SUMMARY:1995 Armenian parliamentary election
DESCRIPTION:Parliamentary elections were held in Armenia on 5 July 1995\, w
 ith a second round on 29 July. There were 150 constituency seats and 40 el
 ected on a national basis using proportional representation. The result wa
 s a victory for the Republic Bloc\, which won 88 of the 190 seats. Overall
  voter turnout was 54.3%.\n\nElection: Armenia\nSource: https://en.wikiped
 ia.org/wiki/1995_Armenian_parliamentary_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-S
