 s)
DESCRIPTION:An independence referendum was held in Bermuda on 16 August 199
 5 for voters to decide whether Bermuda should become an independent sovere
 ign state or remain a British Dependent Territory. On a voter turnout of 5
 9%\, 74% voted against independence. Following the decisive result\, Premi
 er John Swan\, who had been in favour of independence\, resigned.\n\nRefer
 endum: British Overseas Territories\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki
 /1995_Bermudian_independence_referendum\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, 
