DESCRIPTION:Yitzhak Rabin\, the prime minister of Israel\, was assassinated
  on 4 November 1995 at 21:30\, at the end of a rally in support of the Osl
 o Accords at Kings of Israel Square in Tel Aviv. The assailant was Yigal A
 mir\, an Israeli law student and far-right ultranationalist who radically 
 opposed the Oslo Accords and Rabin's peace initiative more broadly.\n\nAss
 assination: Israel\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assassination_of
