SUMMARY:1996 Bulgarian presidential election
DESCRIPTION:Presidential elections were held in Bulgaria on 27 October 1996
 \, with a second round on 3 November. A presidential primary was held earl
 ier in 1996\, which resulted in Petar Stoyanov of the United Democratic Fo
 rces being selected as the candidate of the three largest opposition parti
 es. He won with 59.7% of the vote in the second round.\n\nElection: Bulgar
 ia\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1996_Bulgarian_presidential_elec
 tion\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
