SUMMARY:1996 Lithuanian parliamentary election
DESCRIPTION:Parliamentary elections were held in Lithuania in two stages on
  20 October and 10 November 1996. All 141 seats in the Seimas were up for 
 election\; 70 based on proportional party lists and 71 in single member co
 nstituencies. Where no candidate gained more than 50% of the vote on 20 Oc
 tober\, a run-off was held on 10 November.\n\nElection: Lithuania\nSource:
  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1996_Lithuanian_parliamentary_election\nTex
 t: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
