DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19961128
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19961129
SUMMARY:1996 Algerian constitutional referendum
DESCRIPTION:A constitutional referendum was held in Algeria on 28 November 
 1996. Held amidst the Algerian Civil War\, the amendments would prohibit t
 he use of Islam and ethnic identity in domestic politics. Despite calls fo
 r a boycott\, the amendments were approved by 85.8% of voters with a 79.8%
  turnout. Parliamentary elections were held the following year.\n\nReferen
 dum: Algeria\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1996_Algerian_constitu
 tional_referendum\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.de
 v).
CATEGORIES:Referendum
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1996_Algerian_constitutional_referendum
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
