DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19961128
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19961129
SUMMARY:Sixteenth Amendment of the Constitution of Ireland
DESCRIPTION:The Sixteenth Amendment of the Constitution Act 1996 is an amen
 dment of the Constitution of Ireland which provides that a court can refus
 e bail to a suspect where it feared that while at liberty they would commi
 t a serious criminal offence. It was approved by referendum on 28 November
  1996 and signed into law on 12 December of the same year.\n\nElection: Ir
 eland\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sixteenth_Amendment_of_the_Co
 nstitution_of_Ireland\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.page
 s.dev).
CATEGORIES:Election
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sixteenth_Amendment_of_the_Constitution_o
 f_Ireland
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
