 ber 1997. Prior to the election Prime Minister Thorbjørn Jagland of the L
 abour Party had issued the 36.9 ultimatum declaring that the government wo
 uld step down unless it gained 36.9% of the vote\, the percentage gained b
 y the Labour Party in 1993 under Gro Harlem Brundtland.\n\nElection: Norwa
