SUMMARY:Treaty signed: Good Friday Agreement (United Kingdom)
DESCRIPTION:The Good Friday Agreement or Belfast Agreement is a pair of agr
 eements signed on 10 April 1998 that ended most of the violence of the Tro
 ubles\, an ethnic and national conflict in Northern Ireland since the late
  1960s. It was a major development in the Northern Ireland peace process o
 f the 1990s.\n\nTreaty: United Kingdom\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/w
