SUMMARY:Bülent Ecevit takes power (Turkey)
DESCRIPTION:Mustafa Bülent Ecevit was a Turkish statesman\, poet\, writer\
 , scholar\, and journalist. He served as the Prime Minister of Turkey four
  times between 1974 and 2002\, specifically in 1974\, 1977\, 1978–79\, a
 nd 1999–2002. Ecevit was Chairman of the Republican People's Party (CHP)
  from 1972 to 1980\, and became Chairman of the Democratic Left Party (DSP
 ) in 1987.\n\nNew leader: Turkey\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/B%
 C3%BClent_Ecevit\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev
