SUMMARY:1999 National Assembly for Wales election (United Kingdom)
DESCRIPTION:The inaugural election for the National Assembly for Wales was 
 held on Thursday 6 May 1999 to elect 60 members to the National Assembly f
 or Wales. It was the first devolved general election held in Wales after t
 he successful 1997 Welsh devolution referendum. The election was held alon
 gside the Scottish Parliament election and English local elections.\n\nEle
 ction: United Kingdom\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1999_National
 _Assembly_for_Wales_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jd
