DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19991106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19991107
SUMMARY:1999 Australian republic referendum
DESCRIPTION:The Australian republic referendum held on 6 November 1999 was 
 a two-question referendum to amend the Constitution of Australia. The firs
 t question asked whether Australia should become a republic\, under a bi-p
 artisan appointment model where the president would be appointed by the fe
 deral parliament with a two-thirds majority.\n\nReferendum: Australia\nSou
 rce: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1999_Australian_republic_referendum\nTe
 xt: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
CATEGORIES:Referendum
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1999_Australian_republic_referendum
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
